[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3458077579","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112130#issuecomment-3458077579","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112130","id":3458077579,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OHhOL","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-28T19:09:20Z","updated_at":"2025-10-28T19:09:20Z","body":"> I am using Windows Task Manager to observe the memory usage.\n\nThe Windows Task Manager display is highly irrelevant for this, it is not at all accurate, you always need to monitor your actual app with a profiler.\n\nEven if that was not already the case, even the Windows Task Manager on its own more specialized performance monitors shows both memory and gpu memory are stable with that MRP with zero increase. The entire graph line is flat from start to end.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3458077579/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3458155493","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112130#issuecomment-3458155493","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112130","id":3458155493,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OH0Pl","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-28T19:30:22Z","updated_at":"2025-10-28T19:30:51Z","body":"I can't reproduce this on Linux:\n\n<img width=\"690\" height=\"40\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fe2a89c5-4ab1-4cd2-a901-a3aa208776a0\" />\n\nI've left the MRP running for several minutes (which translates to over 15 minutes of CPU time), and memory usage has remained to 1.2% of total system memory throughout (I have 64 GB of RAM). I had V-Sync disabled and used a tiny window size to get the project to run at 10,000+ FPS, which caused it to run its iterations much faster than normal too.\n\nThis caveat about memory profiling is probably worth mentioning in the documentation still.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3458155493/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3458884363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112130#issuecomment-3458884363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112130","id":3458884363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OKmML","user":{"login":"dstears-git","id":115591712,"node_id":"U_kgDOBuPKIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115591712?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dstears-git","html_url":"https://github.com/dstears-git","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dstears-git/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dstears-git/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dstears-git/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dstears-git/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dstears-git/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dstears-git/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dstears-git/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dstears-git/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dstears-git/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-28T22:59:36Z","updated_at":"2025-10-28T23:46:32Z","body":"Calinou, I don't see the memory usage increase (in task manager) when I disable vsync.\n\nI was able to attach Visual Studio performance profiler to the process and it reports an increase over time at a similar rate to what is reported in Task Manager (with Vsync enabled).\n\n<img width=\"1064\" height=\"204\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0ccd5b87-a4ce-411b-b9e8-c8b2a8c8e479\" />\n\nI admit that I am very much not an expert on this level of debugging. If this is just a matter of Windows Task Manager not accurately reporting app memory usage, then this can be closed. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3458884363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3459203425","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112130#issuecomment-3459203425","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112130","id":3459203425,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OL0Fh","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-29T00:46:44Z","updated_at":"2025-10-29T00:51:20Z","body":"The most plausible way for a constant memory increase would be that something external (e.g. addon / module / tool) keeps a ref from the old texture image data blocking it from ever being freed.\n\nThe NoiseTexture does not anything special compared to most other textures. All it does is bake a new noise image on a thread and when finished uses the RenderingServer.texture_replace() to replace the old texture with a new texture and freeing the old texture.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3459203425/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3459279383","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112130#issuecomment-3459279383","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112130","id":3459279383,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OMGoX","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-29T01:30:47Z","updated_at":"2025-10-29T01:30:47Z","body":"I can reproduce on Windows 11 for a while in many projects. But just when running the project from the editor, not when running standalone, so I'm guessing it's related to the debugger process.\n\nNote that this may not be a leak since debug mode is supposed to use more resources and track things over time.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3459279383/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]